{
   "id": "ITM-AGT-02009-05",
   "archetype_id": "BC-QA-02009",
   "variant_id": null,
   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "The functions \\( f \\) and \\( g \\) are differentiable, with \\( f(4) = 3 \\), \\( f'(4) = 2 \\), \\( g(4) = -3 \\), \\( g'(4) = 4 \\); and \\( f(6) = 3 \\), \\( f'(6) = -2 \\), \\( g(6) = -2 \\), \\( g'(6) = 2 \\). Let \\( h(x) = \\frac{f(x)}{g(x)} \\). Find the value of \\( h'(4) \\)."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": -2
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Record the values at \\( x = 4 \\): \\( f(4) = 3 \\), \\( f'(4) = 2 \\), \\( g(4) = -3 \\), \\( g'(4) = 4 \\).",
         "mathjson": 2
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "By the quotient rule, \\( \\left(\\frac{f}{g}\\right)'(4) = \\frac{f'(4)g(4) - f(4)g'(4)}{[g(4)]^{2}} \\).",
         "mathjson": 3
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Substitute: \\( \\frac{(2)(-3) - (3)(4)}{(-3)^{2}} = \\frac{-18}{9} \\).",
         "mathjson": -2
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "So \\( h'(4) = -2 \\).",
         "mathjson": -2
      }
   ],
